{
"lines": [
"In 1518, a woman in Strasbourg started dancing in the street...",
"and she couldn't stop.",
"She danced for days.",
"Her feet bled.",
"She kept going!",
"Within a month, hundreds of people had joined her!",
"So the city's doctors prescribed...",
"more dancing!",
"They built a stage, and hired musicians!",
"It only got worse.",
"Some accounts say dancers collapsed... and died.",
"Historians now think it was mass hysteria, sparked by famine and fear.",
"It's called the Dancing Plague.",
"And it wasn't the only one."
],
